oracle GNU Make 4.4.1
outcome failure
file Makefile kept 12
| # Under `-q` GNU Make runs the marked lines it meets before the first unmarked
| # one and reads their status. This recipe composes a `$(MAKE)`, so it is cut
| # into segments; each segment carries its per-line launches, so the marked line
| # ahead of the invocation runs while the question is asked and writes its file.
| # The child is then questioned, is not up to date, and the answer is 1 — the
| # recipe's own trailing lines are never reached, exactly as GNU Make stops at
| # the first line it cannot stand in for.
| goal:
| 	+@echo marked-before > before.out
| 	@$(MAKE) --no-print-directory -C sub child
| 	+@echo marked-after > after.out
| 	@echo plain > plain.out
file before.out touched 1
| marked-before
file sub/Makefile kept 1
| child: ; @echo child > child.out
